	abstract = {In France, school dropout and learning in mathematics are two of the main concerns of the National Education Ministry. According to many authors, the presence of depressive symptoms is one of the precursors to the risk of dropping out of school (Blaya, 2010; Fortin & Picard, 1999; Janozs & Leblanc, 1996). Observing the relationship between mathematics learning and depressive characteristics in school would allow an early implementation of school dropout prevention. The purpose of this study is, first, to assess in situ the depressive symptoms with starting primary school children. Secondly, it is about comparing a group of students considered as to be successful or persevering in the field of mathematics to another group seen as being at risk in the same field. The results show a significant difference between them: the presence of depressive symptoms is greater with children at risk of dropping out in mathematics and is therefore an early sign of the school dropout process. © copyright Anae.},
